  "notes": "QC's bright and bouncy bench. The two things the research gives that no other entry on this bench has together are keyboard-written 4-bar progressions and EDM-influenced harmonic instincts, so this model is chordal (three families, no `vamp` weight over the `1_per_bar`/`syncopated_cell` pair) *and* bouncy at the same time — `kick.densityPerBar` [4,6] with `tresilloBias` 0.3, `octaveJumpProb` 0.28, and a snap lane over the layered clap the paragraph names. `major` carries real weight in the scale pool because the research says minor and major both appear; the roman numerals stay minor-mode and the major cuts come out of the scale draw, which is how `_defaults` already handles a mixed-mode model. The hooks are built to be chanted, so melody is `call_response` at moderate density rather than a running line. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium. The inferred parameters are the kick numbers (\"bouncy syncopated kick\" is all the paragraph says) and the melodic register. ⚠ The i–iv–VI–VII family at weight 2 is INFERRED — the research names \"4-bar progressions\" without writing any out for him specifically — and is the first thing to delete if this sounds busier than the records.",
